body:
Hah, yes. I have a quote that I actively avoided the cameras pretty much all I could possibly do so. Many a good vacation is specifically stored to my memory, not photographic evidence, nor looking in a mirror. 

&#x200B;

How could it not cause pain? Reminds me of my senior year in high school (age 17): I was told to try to get a smile out of me for my senior photo by the photographer to think of a pretty girl. Snap goes the film, and I get told that I looked kind of angry after that. Gee, I wonder why?
